Ona ( https://ona.com/?utm_campaign=3Dnewsletter&utm_source=3Dcustomerio&ut=
m_medium=3Demail )

Ramp's agents write 57% of their merged PRs. Here's what they built.

Last week we mapped the background agent tool landscape ( https://backgroun=
d-agents.com/?utm_campaign=3Ddomino-ramp-stripe&utm_source=3Dcustomerio&utm=
_medium=3Demail ). 103 tools across 11 layers. The most common follow-up: w=
hat does it actually take to run a platform for background agents in produc=
tion?

------------------------------------------------------
Ramp's background agents write 57% of their merged PRs
------------------------------------------------------

What Ramp and Stripe built for background agents ( https://ona.com/stories/=
ramp-and-stripe-built-their-background-agent-infrastructure?utm_campaign=3D=
domino-ramp-stripe&utm_source=3Dcustomerio&utm_medium=3Demail )

Stripe's agent platform runs on a remote dev environment they built years b=
efore GPT-3 existed. Ramp hand-rolled theirs on Modal and Cloudflare. Neith=
er started from zero, and both have platform teams maintaining it full-time=
=2E The agent layer came last.

The blog post breaks down what they built across four layers: environments,=
 isolation, connectivity, and automation at scale. The part worth paying at=
tention to is what happens after the first build. Dependencies update, APIs=
 change, integrations break. The surface area grows with every tool you con=
nect. Most companies don't have a platform team to absorb that.

Read the full breakdown =E2=86=92 ( https://ona.com/stories/ramp-and-stripe=
-built-their-background-agent-infrastructure?utm_campaign=3Ddomino-ramp-str=
ipe&utm_source=3Dcustomerio&utm_medium=3Demail )

-----------------------
Listen to the breakdown
-----------------------

We have published a lot on background agents over the past few weeks: the l=
andscape, the Ramp and Stripe architectures, sandboxes, security. It is a l=
ot to keep up with. So we put together a 20-minute audio walkthrough that c=
overs the key points.

Your agents are stuck on your laptop. Here's what Stripe built instead.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

24 min

00:00 | 24:46

------------------------------------------------
We're building a self-driving codebase in public
------------------------------------------------

Starting next week, we're building a fully functioning, open-source app fro=
m scratch, entirely on Ona. No line of code written by a human. Background =
agents planning the architecture, writing code, opening PRs, running CI, fi=
xing what breaks. No demo repo. No curated highlights. The full build, publ=
ic, from commit zero.

We'll run live sessions as we go, document every decision and failure, and =
share regular updates.

We're also giving away 20x $1,000 in credits for teams and engineers that w=
ant to build alongside us. Your codebase or idea, with our support on archi=
tecture and use cases.

Apply for the self-driving codebase project =E2=86=92 ( https://docs.google=
=2Ecom/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdNYonXUK0gOwy2=
NpbqiWOgoyHIyHkFJMy0a6dT3tXJ11tupg/vie=
wform?utm_campaign=3Ddomino-ramp-stripe&utm_source=3Dcustomerio&utm_medium=
=3Demail )

